cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use clerq in your research, please cite it. Earlier versions were
  published as MaxwellBloch; see the reference below for the original package.
title: clerq
abstract: >-
  clerq solves the propagation of classical electromagnetic fields through
  media of open quantum systems, using Maxwell's equations coupled to the
  Lindblad master equation, for example near-resonant light in thermal atomic
  vapours. Formerly MaxwellBloch.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ogden
    given-names: Thomas P.
    email: t@ogden.eu
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tpogden/clerq"
url: "https://clerq.org"
repository-artifact: "https://pypi.org/project/clerq/"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23269881"
keywords:
  - maxwell-bloch equations
  - quantum optics
  - light propagation
  - atomic vapours
  - electromagnetically induced transparency
  - optical solitons
references:
  - type: software
    title: "MaxwellBloch: a Python package for solving the coupled Maxwell-Bloch equations describing the nonlinear propagation of near-resonant light through thermal quantised systems such as atomic vapors"
    authors:
      - family-names: Ogden
        given-names: Thomas P.
    year: 2020
    url: "https://github.com/tpogden/clerq"
    notes: Original release of this package under its former name, MaxwellBloch.
